    <!--
        ScreenBodyService.kt: the lines this file shows on its own — the ball's
        chrome, and the cards it pops when the microphone or the brain is not
        there.

        Every one of these is display-only. The neighbouring Chinese in that
        file is *not*: `meetingMinutesQuery`, `callSummaryQuery`, the
        `LocalBrain.note` stage direction and the todo wake-up prompts are text
        written **to the model**, and the language of a prompt decides the
        language of the answer. They are deliberately left alone — an English
        interface must not become a Chinese reply. See the note at the top of
        `values-en/strings.xml`.

        `%1$s`/`%1$d` are substitutions, not literal text. `ADBKeyboard` and
        `key` stay as they are: they are the name of an app and of a field in
        the settings card, and neither is translated on either side.
    -->
