    <!--
        The two names for a recording that never named itself.

        `meeting_default_title` is written by `MeetingRecorder.start` and read
        back by `ScreenBodyService.meetingMinutesQuery` — one key for both, on
        purpose: the brain is handed the title and the page is laid out under
        the same one, so two literals that drifted apart would show up as a page
        titled one thing and a brain told another.

        `call_default_scene` is the `callSummaryQuery` twin, for an extension
        that registered without a `scene`.

        Both were Kotlin literals until now, which is the same bug in two
        places: the value does reach the screen (it becomes the page title the
        minutes or the summary is laid out under), so on an English tablet it
        read Chinese. They follow the interface language like every other
        displayed string — see `AppLocale`, and the header of
